      "• Limited market evidence: No quantified demand or traction metrics provided.",
      "• Weak revenue/sustainability plan: No mention of pricing, unit economics, or post-launch business model.",
      "• Minimal impact evidence: No demonstration or user testing data to validate 'minimal interference' claims.",
      "• Overconfident risk assessment: Characterizing risks as 'minimal' despite complex manufacturing and safety concerns.",
      "• Thin post-launch plan: Only general feedback solicitation, no support structure."
    ]
