    "Pros": [
      "• All strengths of Project A plus one key enhancement: Planned video demonstration to validate 'minimal interference' claim.",
      "• Stronger evidence plan: Proposed realistic riding scenario video directly addresses critical feasibility concern (wearer visibility).",
      "• Better risk mitigation: Demonstration plan shows proactive approach to proving safety/performance claims.",
      "• Enhanced differentiation: Video evidence would strengthen value proposition against competitors."
    ],
    "Cons": [
      "• Shares all weaknesses of Project A except evidence plan.",
      "• Demonstration is only planned, not yet executed.",
      "• Still lacks market size quantification, detailed roadmap, and revenue model."
    ]
  },
  "Comparison": "Both projects are identical except for Project B's planned demonstration video. This single difference meaningfully improves Project B's position across multiple criteria: 1) It provides concrete evidence for feasibility (criterion 3), 2) strengthens differentiation (criterion 5) by proving the transparency claim, 3) enhances impact evidence (criterion 6), and 4) shows better risk mitigation (criterion 7) by proactively addressing the core safety concern. While both projects share significant weaknesses in market sizing, revenue modeling, and planning detail, Project B's commitment to evidence-based validation gives it a measurable advantage in credibility and risk reduction."
}

